  "description": "Due to budget constraints, I propose to construct the approved extension wall at this stage and complete the remainder of the approved extension at a later date.\n\nAs the property occupies a corner plot, I am also seeking permission to increase the height of the existing boundary garden wall on the side that does not face the main road junction. This would be consistent with the boundary treatment of the neighbouring property opposite. The increased wall height is required to improve privacy and security. The proposal is on the side boundary away from the main road junction and will not adversely affect highway visibility. The wall will be constructed in matching Michelmersh FLB Richmond Facing Brick to ensure it remains in keeping with the character of the property and surrounding area.\n\nIn addition, I am seeking permission to alter the existing garage roof from a flat roof design to a pitched roof, which would mirror that of our neighbours.",
